From the photo, the text is difficult to read. Gold text on a gray 
background doesn't seem to make for good reading. I would have to see what 
the blue version looks like to say for sure, but from the photos I think I 
would prefer something darker.

On Sunday, November 15, 2015 at 3:25:46 PM UTC-8, Robin Powell wrote:
>
>
> Here's what the draft looked like; ignore everything except the 
> cover shots: 
>
> http://users.digitalkingdom.org/~rlpowell/media/public/CLL_grey_proof_pics/ 
>
> It turns out they can't put any writing anywhere except the spine, 
> and that's the only ink color.  If we're going with cloth bound, our 
> choice is what you see in those pictures, or the same thing but with 
> blue binding instead of grey.  That's our *only* choice. 
>
> If we want a dust jacket, someone (presumably Matt Arnold) has to go 
> make it.  I suppose we could give someone money to do so. 
>
> This is the final decision before publication.  Go forth and 
> comment. 
>
>

